      "source": "DeFiHackLabs",
      "text": "Access Control. Lost: $33.6K"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On April 4, 2025, the AIRWA token contract on Binance Smart Chain lost about $33,600 after an attacker exploited a publicly accessible setBurnRate function. The attacker set an extreme burn rate and burned nearly all AIRWA tokens from the liquidity pool, then swapped a small holding for almost all BNB in the pool. The AIRWA token contract's setBurnRate function was deployed without access restrictions. Any user could set an arbitrary burn rate. This made it possible for the attacker to burn nearly all tokens in the liquidity pool, manipulate the token price, and drain most of the pool's BNB."
    }
